###Pure

// ============================================================
// graph (L0) -- the one profile that makes a class an edge
// ============================================================
// A property graph's relationship with properties has no element of its own in Pure: an Association is two
// properties and nothing else. The element that CAN hold a relationship's properties, identity, mapping and
// constraints is a class, and this profile is how a class says it is one (docs/CYPHER_STUDY_2026_10_15.md §5.6).
// Four stereotypes and no tags: nothing in the declaration is a string. The engine and Studio compile the profile
// and its applications as they compile any; legend-lite reads them in phase F (compiler/element/GraphEdges) and
// the Cypher island walks a pattern over an edge class as a navigation through its two ends.
//
//   Edge  on a class: the class is a relationship type; its instances are relationships
//   from  on a to-one class-typed property of the edge class (own, inherited or association-injected): the start node
//   to    likewise: the end node
//   type  on a derived property of the edge class whose body is one spelled enumeration value: the relationship type's
//         name (without it, the class's simple name)
Profile graph::graph
{
   stereotypes: [Edge, from, to, type];
}
